select engine_manual_apply(194,'116b98d1f33815510d46f3cc01f256ae',$p$[{"old": "  - THE OPENING VERDICT WORD OF A RECOMPUTED JUDGMENT IS REPLACED (pkgRHD, ASK 297; Alternate Merge):", "new": "  - THE ENGINE AND THE CHILD HOLD ONE SHARED LIBRARY TEXT, CHECKED BEFORE THE RUN AND AT THE CHILD'S LOAD (ASK 422(a); engine \"Library Sha (ASK 422a)\" and \"Alternate Pass Call\"; child workflow MqQHRl7mQQ0z8QdT, \"Library Check (ASK 422a)\"):\n    - Why: the engine and its child workflow, which runs the second alternate pass, each hold their own Shared Library node. A library change was built, graded, carded and read back twice, and nothing stopped a run whose two copies differed.\n    - The two values: lib_sha is the first 16 hex of SHA-256 over JSON.stringify of the parsed /*LIB*/ line array. map_sha is the first 16 hex of SHA-256 over JSON.stringify of the [key, entry] pairs of the /*MAP*/, keys sorted, each entry from that workflow's own MAP. The child takes all its keys. The engine takes its keys less the named list MAPEXTRA, today [\"REFP\"] (ASK 409), and gives no map_sha unless every listed key is present. So map_sha differs when a shared entry changes, a child key is missing from the engine, an unlisted key is engine-only, or REFP is missing from the engine.\n    - What it does, in the run: \"Library Sha (ASK 422a)\", on the true branch of \"Second Alternate Needed?\" before \"Alternate Pass Call\", computes both values at run time from the engine's own Shared Library; no value is stored as a constant, so a hand edit of the engine copy is caught too. \"Alternate Pass Call\" sends lib_sha and map_sha in pass, not in sa. In the child, \"Library Check (ASK 422a)\", between \"Alternate Pass In\" and \"Alternate Pass Check\", computes both from the child's own library and stops the child with \"pkgLIB1: library drift, engine lib <x> map <y>, child lib <x> map <y>\" unless both pairs are equal; when they are, it passes on lib422, which names all four values.\n    - What a stop costs: \"Alternate Pass Call\" continues on error, and Pass Accumulate marks that pass's seats \"[AUDIT v21: ALTERNATE TRIED ... NOT SEATED]\" with the reason \"sub-workflow error: pkgLIB1: library drift ...\". The removed seat keeps its round 1 body, and the run goes on. So a drift costs that pass's second alternate, and the report says why.\n    - Before the run and after a write: the child runs only when a second alternate pass is needed, so the load check runs seldom. The run-start check (ASK 419, runstart.py, check 3) fetches both workflows and refuses to release a run unless both values are equal; it prints \"3 map_sha equal <x>\" or \"3 MAP DIFFERS: engine <x>, child <y>\". The readback script libsha.py prints the body, header and map_sha of each workflow and says EQUAL only when both values are equal. A library change is written to both workflows by the one writer, libw.py.\n    - Shown offline: on the target texts, the live pair passes; each of one changed /*LIB*/ line, an unreadable engine library, a pass without lib_sha, one shared MAP entry changed in the child (lib_sha equal), a child key dropped from the engine, an unlisted engine-only key, and REFP missing from the engine stops the child. The plain-JS SHA-256 equals node crypto on the targets and on a live fetch. The run-start check refuses a child whose MAP has one entry changed and whose library lines are equal, on \"3 MAP DIFFERS\" alone.\n    - Live: engine 1861543f (from 040e0e02), saved 23:56:49Z on 11-18; child c226d9cb (from a9229af9), saved 23:56:53Z on 11-18; lib_sha 5b8a26a88fc94b12 and map_sha ad61e1e3658dd351 on both.\n    - Limits: two copies still exist in n8n; a hand edit of one in the editor is caught at the next run start or child load, not when it is made. Not shown by a run; its marks are no pkgLIB1 stop, and, when a second alternate pass runs, lib422 in the child execution naming both pairs of values.\n  - THE OPENING VERDICT WORD OF A RECOMPUTED JUDGMENT IS REPLACED (pkgRHD, ASK 297; Alternate Merge):"}]$p$::jsonb,null,null,null,null,null,false) r;